)PANEL KEYLIST(ISRHELP,ISR)
)ATTR DEFAULT(%+_)
/*********************************************************************/
/* PANEL    : MBKRTH                                                 */
/* TITLE    : HELP - INTEREST RATE CHANGES                           */
/*-------------------------------------------------------------------*/
/* 2010-04-12 AOS  ORIGINAL                                          */
/* 2020-03-11 RKS  BANK RATE MASS-CHANGE PROCEDURE                   */
/*********************************************************************/
  % TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE) SKIP(ON)
  + TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN) SKIP(ON)
  ] TYPE(TEXT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) SKIP(ON)
)BODY EXPAND(//) WIDTH(80)
%TUTORIAL -/-/- INTEREST RATE CHANGES -/-/- TUTORIAL
%Command ===>_ZCMD                                                             +
+
+One entry = one rate on one product.  INRAT010%announces+the change
+(writes MBK.PRD.INT.RATEPEND and the customer notices) and%applies+it to
+the product on the effective date.  Accounts on negotiated rates are not
+changed - they are listed for relationship managers.
+
]Rate types+
+  %C+credit tier 1-5   %B+bonus rate   %A+arranged OD   %U+unarranged OD
+
]Reason codes+
+  %BOER+Bank of England Bank Rate change  %MKTR+market / funding cost
+  %PRDR+product review (Pricing Committee) %CMPT+competitor response
+  %CORR+correction of an earlier change    %NPRD+new product (INRAT010 use)
+
]Notice+
+   A lower savings rate or a higher overdraft rate needs 14 days notice.
+   INRAT010 rejects it otherwise - unless%Base rate tracker+is Y (the
+   product terms let the rate follow Bank Rate immediately).
+
]Bank Rate day procedure+
+   1. Key every tracker product with the same effective date, reason
+      BOER and tracker Y - the screen keeps those fields between entries.
+   2. A second user approves the whole list (option A, line command A).
+   3. RELEASE on the approval list writes the file and submits INRAT01.
)PROC
  &ZUP = MBKMENUH
)END
